  "verdict": "Level A: decision-trained's edge over MSE-trained did NOT reach significance on real MPPI elites (mean +0.0890, p=0.736, 19/35 non-tied wins, 45/80 seeds tied) -- the edge SHRINKS TO NOISE (or reverses) under low-diversity real candidates.\nReference: on the synthetic hybrid-family test the same weights scored a zero-fill->mse gap of +0.9711; on real elites the comparable gap is +0.6346 -- the candidate set itself carries much less rankable signal, consistent with CLAIMS.md's C1 live-elite finding that real elites are low-diversity (~1/5 of hybrid's path spread) and erode a derivative-based edge.\nLevel B (fill-in-the-loop): no significant edge for decision-trained once the planner itself plans on the filled map (mean +0.3152, p=0.314) -- coupling candidate generation to the fill erodes the edge further than level A alone.",
